    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0823" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6178.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-18T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1913—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Your February 15, 11 p.m. Your six agreements with General Huerta and the
                    President cause no less satisfaction to the Department than to the American
                    colony in Mexico City; the Department congratulates you upon your excellent
                    work; also upon initiating and carrying out the measures mentioned in the latter
                    part of your February 15, 7 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
